title: 'statement-store: avoid blocking the event loop during propagation'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    Statement propagation no longer awaits each notification inline: sends are queued as
    futures driven by the protocol's main event loop, so an unresponsive peer stalls only its
    own send. Also fixes a network error being reported as a successful send on the initial
    sync path, which marked statements as known to a peer that never received them.
- audience: Node Operator
  description: |-
    New counters `substrate_sync_statement_send_failures_total` and
    `substrate_sync_statement_undelivered_total`, both labelled by `reason` with the values
    `network`, `timeout` and `no_sink`. Send timeouts are now logged at `warn`.
crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: patch
